### Muonic X-rays of muons stopped in the target, one job (scripts/muonic_xray.sh runs several).
### Needs the aliases muxSeed, muxEvents, muxDir, muxFile, muxGeometry (geometry macro, e.g.
### macro/geom_target_al.mac), muxHalf (half size of the source plane, cm), muxWorld (world size in
### x and y, cm; at least 2 x muxHalf), muxEmin and muxEmax (GeV).
### EXPACS mu+ and mu- with kinetic energies muxEmin - muxEmax from a horizontal plane at z = 112 cm
### (11 cm above the 10 cm lead layer), zenith < 75 deg. The band only speeds the run up: the live
### time is that of the band, so rates are right as long as no muon outside it stops in the volumes
### studied (0.1 - 2 GeV covers every stop in Al in a full-spectrum test). Only events with a photon
### of a mu- capture are written (/EventFilter 5): columns mux_* (energy at creation and when leaving
### the volume it was born in, time, place, source 0 muonic X-ray / 1 nuclear-capture gamma).

/tof/det/worldSize {muxWorld} {muxWorld} 300 cm
/control/execute {muxGeometry}

/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 5
/OutputDirectory {muxDir}
/OutputFile {muxFile}
/gun/seed {muxSeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 2
/tof/cosmic/model expacs
/tof/cosmic/species mu+ mu-
/tof/cosmic/angular all 2 mu+ guan mu- guan
/tof/cosmic/planeCenter 0 0 112 cm
/tof/cosmic/halfX {muxHalf} cm
/tof/cosmic/halfY {muxHalf} cm
/tof/cosmic/thetaMax 75 deg
/tof/cosmic/energyMin {muxEmin} GeV
/tof/cosmic/energyMax {muxEmax} GeV
/run/beamOn {muxEvents}
